From: Antigravity AI Team <dev@antigravity.ai>
Subject: [PATCH 0001/0003] arm64: dts: s905w: adjust CMA codec memory allocation to 224MB

Adjust codec_mm_cma reservation from 208MB to 224MB (229376 KiB)
to eliminate SCATTER_MEM allocation failures during 4K HEVC / H.264
hardware decoding while preserving system RAM for Android OS.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity AI Team <dev@antigravity.ai>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905w-stv3000.dts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905w-stv3000.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905w-stv3000.dts
index a1b2c34..d5e6f78 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905w-stv3000.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/meson-gxl-s905w-stv3000.dts
@@ -45,8 +45,8 @@
 	codec_mm_cma: linux,codec_mm_cma {
 		compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 		reusable;
-		size = <0x0 0x0d000000>; /* 208 MB */
+		size = <0x0 0x0e000000>; /* 224 MB (229376 KiB) */
 		alignment = <0x0 0x400000>;
 	};
 };
-- 
2.34.1
